+# Institution separation — Vantoris X Money source
+
+Recovery date: 18 November 2026.
+
+## What was recovered
+
+The complete runnable member application was not on `main` (`792cfa32`, 22 files). It is on `migration/remove-base44-and-codex` at `11ec54f9067db3e8c24bf4b026daf2062a7d5978` (431 files): member and staff sign-in, TOTP, PostgreSQL migrations `000`–`024`, internal transfers, and the member interface.
+
+`recovery/merge-vantoris-live` at `d0a68dd` is the same member application minus that independent runtime, still tied to Base44, and mixed with AVCU-labelled tests. It was not merged.
+
+## How the institutions are separated
+
+| Institution | Where it stays | What this branch does |
+|---|---|---|
+| Vantoris X Money | This branch, `work/xmoney-separated-source` | Product name, package, and visible brand |
+| Vantoris Private Institution | Unchanged branch `migration/remove-base44-and-codex` | Not relabelled in place |
+| AVCU | Its own repositories (`avcu`, `avcreditunion`, `American-Vanguard-credit-union`) | `avcu_*` migration filenames kept for checksum history only |
+| Ashcombe Private Bank | `iamtheoracle/ashcombe-private-bank` | No Ashcombe schema, client, or brand in this tree |
+| Group Headquarters | `iamtheoracle/vantoris-corporate` and `iamtheoracle/vantoriss` | No group authority over this ledger |
+
+## What is not a recovered record
+
+- The Hambros tribute is a public historical note with an explicit non-affiliation statement. It is not an X Money client or office.
+- Founder stories name Madam C. J. Walker, Sara Blakely, and James Dyson, with public source links. They are not Vantoris people. Colton Hogan and GGM were not in this source.
+- No live member register or statement file was in Git. Balances are not invented here.
+- This branch is not merged, not deployed, and not an operating payment service.
+
+## Ledger rule
+
+Posted balances remain sums of the existing `vantoris_ledger` journals. The schema name is historical. It does not grant Ashcombe, AVCU, Vantoris Private Institution, or Group Headquarters access to these rows.
